# Testing

Do not assume a test runner. Check `package.json`; if none exists, ask before adding one.

## Requirements
- New logic ships with tests in the same change. Bug fixes ship with a regression test that fails before the fix.
- **Must be unit-tested** (pure functions, no network):
  - each rule in the rule-based scam engine (positive case, negative case, edge case),
  - trust-score calculation and flag-weight aggregation,
  - anti-gaming checks (rate limit, burst detection, new-account clustering),
  - LLM output schema validation (valid, malformed, missing fields, extra fields),
  - skill-gap computation (matching, synonyms/normalization, empty CV, empty JD),
  - Kanban stage transition logic.
- **Integration tests** for API endpoints: success, validation error, unauthenticated, forbidden, rate-limited.
- **RLS tests**: user A cannot read/update/delete user B's CVs, applications, or flags; admin-only operations reject normal users.
- **Never call the real LLM in automated tests.** Use a mock/fake provider with fixed fixtures. Real-LLM runs belong only to the evaluation scripts (see `40-thesis-quality.mdc`).
- Tests must be deterministic: no reliance on wall-clock time, randomness, or network (inject clock/RNG).
- Test names describe behavior: `flags_from_new_accounts_are_frozen_when_burst_detected`.
- Do not delete or weaken a failing test to get green. Explain the failure instead.

## Frontend testing
- Test behavior via accessible queries (role, label, text), not implementation details.
- Cover loading, empty, error, success states, and the scam warning banner (shows evidence, accessible).

## Manual test checklist (include relevant items in your "How to test it")
- [ ] Sign up / log in with email+password; log in with OAuth; log out.
- [ ] Add a job manually; add a job by pasting a link; metadata (company, position, date) auto-saved.
- [ ] Drag a card between stages; reload; position/stage persists. Keyboard alternative works.
- [ ] Upload/save a CV; create a new version; select a version for analysis.
- [ ] Save a JD -> skills JSON appears; run skill-gap with a chosen CV.
- [ ] Paste a clearly fake JD ("payment required", "high salary no experience") -> warning banner with evidence.
- [ ] Paste a normal JD -> no false warning.
- [ ] Simulate LLM failure -> card still saved, rules still run, AI status shows unavailable + retry.
- [ ] Flag a JD/Company; flag weight updates; duplicate flag by same user rejected.
- [ ] Rapid repeated flagging -> rate limited (429) and shown clearly.
- [ ] Many fresh accounts flagging one JD -> flags frozen, appear in admin queue.
- [ ] Admin can review, release/reject frozen flags, edit blacklist; normal user cannot access admin pages/APIs.
- [ ] User A cannot see user B's data (try direct URL/ID access).
- [ ] No API keys visible in browser network tab, bundle, or source.
